; Limit 08: the runtime sits underneath the builtins it would implement.
; Blocks the division itself in job 2 (l0_div, l0_mod).
;
; This program type checks. The limit is in what it compiles to: the builtin
; div lowers to `call i64 @l0_div`, the C runtime function this code is meant
; to replace (spec section 10.3). L0 has no division that lowers to the bare
; sdiv/srem instruction, so an L0 l0_div can check for zero but has nothing to
; divide with. See 08-unchecked-division.ir.txt for the emitted IR.

(def l0_div ((a int) (b int)) int
  (div a b))

(def main ((input (list int))) int
  (l0_div 7 2))
